1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,124
In the last class, you moved a crew's standing in one sitting.

2
00:00:04,924 --> 00:00:06,780
A campaign asks something harder.

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,269
How fast does it move,

4
00:00:09,719 --> 00:00:11,740
and what does it open when it gets there?

5
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:17,165
Today you'll build a door that only trust can open.

6
00:00:18,065 --> 00:00:21,162
And then a way for the crew to slam it on themselves.

7
00:00:22,362 --> 00:00:26,132
First, what actually moves standing over weeks.

8
00:00:26,582 --> 00:00:27,897
I measured every row.

9
00:00:29,697 --> 00:00:31,365
Finishing a side's job.

10
00:00:31,815 --> 00:00:34,463
Five points, or ten for the harder kind.

11
00:00:35,363 --> 00:00:36,780
Paying the levy in a hail.

12
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:39,488
Twenty points, for a hundred credits.

13
00:00:41,288 --> 00:00:43,641
And now look at the last row.

14
00:00:44,541 --> 00:00:47,024
A step of the story can carry a deed as well.

15
00:00:48,824 --> 00:00:50,748
I put one on a lead and finished it,

16
00:00:51,198 --> 00:00:53,932
and the standing went from forty to fifty-one.

17
00:00:54,832 --> 00:00:56,294
But a step is finished once.

18
00:00:57,494 --> 00:01:01,462
That gives you two tools, and most of this lecture is the second one.

19
00:01:03,262 --> 00:01:05,942
A prize is a deed on a step.

20
00:01:06,842 --> 00:01:09,573
It's given once, on the evening you choose.

21
00:01:11,373 --> 00:01:13,567
Everything else, the crew can do again.

22
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:15,953
Jobs can be taken again,

23
00:01:16,403 --> 00:01:18,177
and answers can be given again.

24
00:01:19,977 --> 00:01:22,629
So on those you put a price,

25
00:01:23,079 --> 00:01:25,795
in credits or in time.

26
00:01:26,695 --> 00:01:30,058
And you decide how much of each an evening pays.

27
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:33,379
So here's a door, in three parts.

28
00:01:35,179 --> 00:01:38,114
A lead the crew can see from the very first evening.

29
00:01:38,564 --> 00:01:40,473
It tells them what opens it.

30
00:01:41,373 --> 00:01:44,483
That matters, because a door nobody knows about

31
00:01:44,933 --> 00:01:46,628
isn't a reason to do anything.

32
00:01:48,428 --> 00:01:49,996
So under a heading,

33
00:01:50,446 --> 00:01:51,666
I list the keys.

34
00:01:52,566 --> 00:01:54,595
Each line starts with a hyphen,

35
00:01:55,045 --> 00:01:57,169
and a small icon where the dot would be.

36
00:01:58,069 --> 00:01:59,512
A handshake for the levy,

37
00:01:59,962 --> 00:02:01,304
a flag for the jobs,

38
00:02:01,754 --> 00:02:05,453
and a crossed circle for the one thing that shuts it.

39
00:02:07,253 --> 00:02:09,753
Then one answer in the Compact's hail.

40
00:02:10,653 --> 00:02:14,482
After the key it says, if standing is forty or more.

41
00:02:14,932 --> 00:02:16,880
Below that, the button isn't there.

42
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,162
And the record it leads to,

43
00:02:20,612 --> 00:02:22,349
where they're finally told.

44
00:02:23,549 --> 00:02:25,422
Why forty, and not some other number?

45
00:02:27,222 --> 00:02:29,882
At twenty it opens after one levy,

46
00:02:30,332 --> 00:02:32,791
on the first evening, and that isn't a door.

47
00:02:33,691 --> 00:02:36,131
At sixty, a crew may never get there.

48
00:02:37,931 --> 00:02:40,761
At forty, a crew that takes one job a week

49
00:02:41,211 --> 00:02:42,750
and pays the levy once

50
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,938
arrives in about the fourth week.

51
00:02:45,838 --> 00:02:47,711
And that's where I want them to hear it,

52
00:02:48,161 --> 00:02:49,483
right before the act ends.

53
00:02:51,283 --> 00:02:53,816
So you choose the number by choosing the week.

54
00:02:55,016 --> 00:02:57,421
A door that only opens is a reward.

55
00:02:57,871 --> 00:02:59,841
A door that can close is a story.

56
00:03:01,641 --> 00:03:04,778
So in the Gleaners' hail, I add one tempting answer.

57
00:03:05,678 --> 00:03:07,807
Sell them a copy of the Count.

58
00:03:09,607 --> 00:03:11,287
It earns the Gleaners' respect,

59
00:03:11,737 --> 00:03:15,687
and in the same breath it costs the Compact's trust.

60
00:03:16,587 --> 00:03:19,070
An answer with one side can do a deed with another.

61
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:21,824
Here's what I measured.

62
00:03:22,274 --> 00:03:25,286
Forty with the Compact became seventeen.

63
00:03:26,186 --> 00:03:28,317
And at home, three things changed.

64
00:03:29,217 --> 00:03:31,853
The greeting went cold, the manifest was gone,

65
00:03:32,303 --> 00:03:34,251
and so was the better work.

66
00:03:35,451 --> 00:03:37,329
Now you plan it.

67
00:03:38,229 --> 00:03:40,824
The ledger is one row for each evening,

68
00:03:41,274 --> 00:03:42,938
with the standing you expect,

69
00:03:43,388 --> 00:03:45,369
and the door you expect to open.

70
00:03:47,169 --> 00:03:49,873
The numbers are a guess, and the crew won't follow them.

71
00:03:50,773 --> 00:03:52,883
What matters is the last column.

72
00:03:54,683 --> 00:03:56,617
For each door, you've named an evening,

73
00:03:57,067 --> 00:03:59,419
and you can check the price against the wages.

74
00:04:00,319 --> 00:04:03,326
Too cheap, and it opens on night one.

75
00:04:03,776 --> 00:04:06,019
Too dear, and it never does.

76
00:04:07,819 --> 00:04:09,922
And remember where all of this is kept.

77
00:04:10,372 --> 00:04:12,874
It's in the ship's own record, in the save.

78
00:04:14,074 --> 00:04:15,681
Lint's clean, so here it is.

79
00:04:17,481 --> 00:04:19,790
Three answers, and no manifest.

80
00:04:20,690 --> 00:04:22,375
I pay the levy twice,

81
00:04:22,825 --> 00:04:24,316
and now there are four.

82
00:04:26,116 --> 00:04:28,481
I ask, and the lead is done.

83
00:04:30,281 --> 00:04:32,156
Then out to the breaking yard,

84
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:34,178
and I sell the Count.

85
00:04:35,078 --> 00:04:37,388
Nothing tells me what that cost.

86
00:04:39,188 --> 00:04:41,889
Back home, the good work has gone from the list.

87
00:04:42,789 --> 00:04:45,217
And the hail's down to three answers again.

88
00:04:46,417 --> 00:04:49,206
So you award standing once, on a step,

89
00:04:49,656 --> 00:04:51,584
and you price the rest.

90
00:04:53,384 --> 00:04:55,792
Every answer that earns it gets a cost.

91
00:04:56,692 --> 00:04:58,784
And all of it lives in the ship's record,

92
00:04:59,234 --> 00:05:01,445
which the save carries from week to week.

93
00:05:03,245 --> 00:05:06,899
Next time, we look at the act from the crew's side of the table.
